                      "id": "candidate-02",
                      "version": "agent.2",
                      "label": "Fold scalar multiplies into one add-with-alpha kernel (6 -> 4 elementwise kernels)",
                      "title": "Fold scalar multiplies into one add-with-alpha kernel (6 -> 4 elementwise kernels)",
                      "hypothesis": "Because 1.25*x + 0.75*y - 0.125 is algebraically identical to 1.25*(x + 0.6*y) - 0.125, torch.add(x, y, alpha=0.6) computes the scaled sum in a single kernel, eliminating the separate y*0.75 operand kernel that both the baseline and candidate-01 paid for. With launch overhead dominating at 8192 elements, dropping one kernel should reduce p50 by roughly one op's worth of overhead versus candidate-01's 13.312us.",
                      "change": "run(inputs) now does: out = torch.add(inputs['x'], inputs['y'], alpha=0.6); out.mul_(1.25); out.sub_(0.125); return out.clamp_min_(0). 4 elementwise kernels, zero temporaries beyond the single output tensor, no clone, inputs untouched. get_inputs/get_test_cases/get_benchmark_inputs/reference are byte-identical to the baseline.",
